[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   step_070: Galactic-tide insertion -- the last unsubtracted Newtonian
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   channel.
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   The planetary baseline (steps 040/042/063/064) subtracts the measured
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   kick budget of the Solar system, and the Planet Nine insertion (step
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   062) shows the published perturber cannot rotate the catalogued
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   trajectories.  One Newtonian channel remains unevaluated on the real
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   trajectories: the Galactic tide, the dominant long-term perturber of
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   Oort-cloud comets.  Its strength at the 250 AU boundary sphere is small
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   -- the vertical tide coefficient 4 pi G rho ~ 5.6e-15 yr^-2 against
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   the solar GM/r^2 ~ 6.3e-4 AU yr^-2 -- but the anomaly itself is also
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   small (~0.1 deg), so the tide's actual contribution is measured here
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   directly rather than asserted negligible.
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   Method
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   The identical bidirectional integration of step_063 is rerun with the
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   Heisler & Tremaine (1986) tidal tensor added as an external potential
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   via Strang splitting (kick-drift-kick on WHFast).  In the
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   epoch-fixed approximation -- each leg spans ~600 yr, vastly less than
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   the ~240 Myr galactic period -- the inertial-frame tensor is
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   a_gal = ( +OmG^2 x,  -OmG^2 y,  -4 pi G rho z )
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   in galactic coordinates (x toward the Galactic centre, z toward the
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   north Galactic pole), with OmG = A - B = 26 km/s/kpc (A = -B = 13,
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   delta = 0) and rho = 0.1 Msun/pc^3 (Levison et al. 2001 convention).
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   Each comet's two legs are integrated with and without the tide; the
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   per-leg boundary periapsis-direction offset and the change in the
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   orig->fut rotation are measured on the catalogued trajectories, and
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   the cap contrast of the tide-induced contribution is tested.
[2026-09-21 14:48:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 070]   Outputs
